.TH SAPHIRA-ACCOUNTS-BOOTSTRAP 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
saphira-accounts-bootstrap \- one-time legacy accounts.json bootstrap
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-accounts-bootstrap
.RB [ --write ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira-accounts-bootstrap
crossed r48 to r49 and is otherwise retired: the first account-aware
signer reconstructed its registry only via a full census, which
fails closed on historical fragment-carrying NVRs that predate the
registry. This tool performs that census once per repository ahead
of publication (payload declarations recovered from published bytes,
validated with the deployed makepkg parser and the signer's own
union rules) and atomically emits the exact registry schema.
.PP
Default is dry-run (validates everything, writes nothing).
.B --write
emits. Refuses if the registry exists, if a signer lock is held, or
in an r49 (database) world. It never signs, publishes, moves APKs,
rewrites indexes, renames staged transactions, or reads Git or the
recipe tree. Must be run as root; use sudo explicitly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --write
Emit the registries (default is dry-run).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /out/stage4/packages/<generation>/$ARCH/accounts.json
Emitted once, then frozen as migration evidence.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Validated (dry-run) or emitted.
.TP
.B 1
Refusal, validation failure, or not root.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
sudo saphira-accounts-bootstrap
.br
sudo saphira-accounts-bootstrap --write
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira (7),
.BR sign-apk-repo (8),
.BR saphira-repo-state (8),
.BR saphira-repo-migrate (8),
.BR ensure-identity (8)
